==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suf|en|shit|y|id2=adjectival}}. Cognate with {{cog|nds-de|schittig|t=dirty, shitty}}, {{cog|de|Scheißig|t=shitty}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈʃɪti/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈʃɪti/|[ˈʃɪɾi]}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-shitty.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪti|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{lb|en|vulgar|colloquial}} Very bad; [[unpleasant]]; [[miserable]]; [[insignificant]].
#: {{ux|en|The television I bought there was so '''shitty''' that I will never shop there again.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'm feeling '''shitty''' today; I don't want to go out.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1988 November|author=Byron Coley|title=Underground|journal=[[w:Spin (magazine)|Spin]]|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=4ffg2qNLJucC&pg=PA101&lpg=PA101&dq=%22shittier%7Cshittiest%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&source=bl&ots=AM18gVBVrc&sig=h1SHYfHQ47W_wML8Wqo7XhLEwKs&hl=en&sa=X&ei=SthEULS0BNHvmAWwzYCIAw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22shittier%7Cshittiest%22%20australia%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=101|text=It's a well-known fact that reading is about the '''shittiest''' thing you can do for your eyes.}}
#* {{RQ:Noire Thug-A-Licious|page=128|passage=Except for Rasheena, the rest of the baby mamas was at least struggling to live halfway right. They used to clown and act '''shitty''' whenever they came by Noojie's and saw Carmiesha there. But every last one of them ended up being grateful to her for the things she did for their kids.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=[[w:Everett True|Everett True]]|title=Nirvana: The True Story|year_published=2009|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=H89kHhJR4-AC&pg=PT508&lpg=PT508&dq=%22shittier%7Cshittiest%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&source=bl&ots=BvBTWSrcPv&sig=INwoicfh9MJ8kfWiJ1LNaW9G_fE&hl=en&sa=X&ei=SthEULS0BNHvmAWwzYCIAw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22shittier%7Cshittiest%22%20australia%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|text=The difference is they usually have a '''shittier''' singer, and no originality.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Rik Leaf|title=Four Homeless Millionaires|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=OsECnpJIDQEC&pg=PA134&lpg=PA134&dq=%22shittier%7Cshittiest%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&source=bl&ots=TxEi1986KR&sig=JJaQzmjwLY7Skv5Ba1lG6Hi9W1M&hl=en&sa=X&ei=SthEULS0BNHvmAWwzYCIAw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22shittier%7Cshittiest%22%20australia%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=134|text=Halfway there we turned off the highway onto possibly the '''shittiest''' gravel road I have ever driven. In Canada, we would call it washboard; in Australia they call it corrugated, but you get the point.}}
# {{lb|en|US|vulgar|slang|not comparable}} Under the [[influence]] of [[illicit]] [[drugs]] or [[alcohol]]; [[drunk]]; [[high]].
# {{lb|en|UK|Australia|South East|regional|NZ|vulgar|slang}} Annoyed.
#: {{ux|en|Don't get '''shitty''' with me!}}
# {{lb|en|vulgar}} Covered in [[faeces]]/[[feces]]; [[feculent]].
# {{lb|en|informal|vulgar}} Of low [[quality]] or [[standard]]; [[inferior]]; not [[up to par]], or failing one's expectations
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=Curtis Sittenfeld|title=Prep: A Novel|page=157|text=“She's a '''shitty''' teacher, but Ault was in a bind.” But she hadn't been a '''shitty''' teacher when she'd been hired. She'd never taught before. And who was Aspeth to decide she was '''shitty''' now? She was still inexperienced.}}

